cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived artifacts, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Provenance Confounding in Image Authenticity Classification:
  code and analysis pipeline
abstract: >-
  Code, data pipeline and manuscript sources for a study of class-conditional
  provenance confounding: when the two classes of an authenticity-classification
  image dataset are sourced by different procedures, the label predicts the
  acquisition process rather than the property being labeled, and no
  in-distribution evaluation can detect it. Contains the data pipeline, four
  model families, external evaluation on two independently captured
  distributions, a label-free normalization operator with per-axis, per-constant
  and per-order ablations, a five-seed variance sweep, calibration and two
  independent attribution analyses, and a provenance audit run across four
  application areas. Contains no images.
type: software
